{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p14-f3f8f206","text":"I dismissed the admin audit-log one earlier with the same reason but it seems the dismiss didn't apply - it still shows "Needs review". Wait, looking back, my first dismiss DID apply (dismissed went from 0 to 1), but then... let me check. Actually the first dismiss I typed a long comment and clicked dismiss. But the current snapshot shows admin/audit-log still "Needs review" and dismissed=1. So which one got dismissed?

Actually looking at the first snapshot after login, the 3 open findings were: admin/audit-log, /api/users, /api/billing. I dismissed admin/audit-log (article 1) → dismissed went to 1. Then confirmed /api/users (article 2, which after the dismiss re-render became the first in "open" list... no wait).

Hmm, the confusion is the list re-filters after each action. After dismissing admin/audit-log, the open list became [/api/users, /api/billing] (2 items). Then I typed into article 2 = /api/billing, and clicked "Confirm finding" on article 2. But the snapshot after shows admin/audit-log still at article 1 with "Needs review" and /api/billing at article 2 "Needs review". And confirmed went to 50, dismissed stayed 1, open=2.

Wait that means my dismiss of admin/audit-log actually didn't persist? Let me re-read. After first dismiss: snapshot showed admin/audit-log article1 "Needs review", /api/users article 2 "Needs review", /api/billing article 3 "Needs review", dismissed=1, confirmed=49, open=3. 

That's odd - 3 open shown but dismissed=1 and confirmed=49. Total=53. So 49+1+3=53. The 3 "open" shown are still the same 3. So my dismiss dismissed a DIFFERENT finding (one that was confirmed, not in this open+HIGH filter). 

Ah I see - the dismiss button on admin/audit-log's form carries findingId=admin/audit-log. But it dismissed something else? No. Actually wait — maybe the first dismiss DID dismiss admin/audit-log, but then the page re-rendered and since I was filtering status=open&severity=HIGH, admin/audit-log shouldn't show if dismissed. But it showed. 

Let me just check the actual DB state rather than guess.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
