VibeCheck is a productized security-audit service for teams shipping AI-generated
("vibe-coded") software: an automated scanning engine (OWASP-mapped static rules, secrets
detection, dependency/license review, and a 29-check AI-code + MCP ruleset), a **mandatory
analyst review gate**, a client portal with remediation tracking, re-scan regression
comparison, and test-mode billing.

This repository is a working end-to-end prototype against the PRD (v1.0). It runs as a
single Next.js app with Postgres.

## Quick start

```bash
npm install
createdb vibecheck            # once; DATABASE_URL defaults to postgres://localhost:5432/vibecheck
cp .env.example .env.local    # adjust DATABASE_URL if needed
npm run db:push               # create schema
npm run db:seed               # demo tenants, audits, review queues
npm run dev                   # http://localhost:3000 (or: npm run dev -- --port 3210)
```

### Demo accounts

| Role | Email | Password | Sees |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Analyst | `analyst@vibecheck.dev` | `Analyst123!` | Review queue, triage desk, ruleset, reports |
| Client (Acme) | `client@acme.dev` | `Client123!` | Delivered audit, remediation tracker, billing |
| Client (Northwind) | `client@northwind.dev` | `Client123!` | Live review queue engagement, upgrade flow |
| Admin (operator) | `admin@vibecheck.dev` | `Admin123!` | All engagements, clients, audit log |

## Verification

```bash
npm run typecheck        # tsc --noEmit
npm test                 # 11 tests: scanner accuracy + review/finalization gates
npm run scan:benchmark   # vulnerable fixture: 53 findings / 29-of-29 rules; clean fixture: 0 findings (0 FPs)
npm run build            # production build, 17 routes
npm run purge:sources    # retention job: deletes client source after SOURCE_RETENTION_DAYS (default 30)
```

The benchmark fixtures live in `benchmarks/vulnerable-app` (seeded vulnerabilities across
every rule family) and `benchmarks/clean-app` (hardened; must produce zero findings).

## Documentation

- [Technical architecture](docs/architecture.md) — stack, data model, scan pipeline, gates
- [Analyst runbook](docs/analyst-runbook.md) — operating the review desk end to end
- [Client help](docs/client-help.md) — portal usage for clients
- [Prototype scope & limitations](docs/prototype-scope.md) — what is simulated vs production-ready

## Key behaviors enforced in code (not just UI)

- **FR-10 hard gate:** `canFinalizeReport()` in `src/lib/review.ts` blocks finalization
  server-side unless a scan succeeded, every finding has an analyst decision, the review is
  signed off, and the report is a draft. Finalized reports are immutable; triage resets sign-off.
- **Terms gate:** clients cannot view a final report or track remediation until they accept
  the service terms (`/terms`); acceptance is written to the audit log.
- **Tenant isolation:** every engagement/report query is scoped by `orgId` server-side;
  clients receive 404 for other tenants' data and drafts.
- **Secret redaction:** every finding snippet passes through `src/lib/scan/redact.ts` — raw
  credentials are never stored or shown.
- **Auditability:** findings/report/billing/scan events write to `audit_logs` with actor,
  org, engagement, and detail.
- **Retention:** `scripts/purge-sources.ts` deletes retained source snapshots after the
